-- title:
--   Supersingular chart with q+1 ends, Drinfeld quotient, tame inertia
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ and $\ell$ are primes, $M'$ a nonzero natural number, and the arithmetic hypotheses are: $q \nmid M'$, $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$.
--
--   **Level data.** $L$ is a field of characteristic zero, $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and `hι` asserts the existence of a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$. The subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times}$ is required (`hH₁`) to be the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^{\times}$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^{\times}$; thus $H_1$ consists of the units that are $\equiv 1$ both modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell$. The field $K$ is an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$, required (`hK`) to be [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the subfield of $L(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   **Base ring.** $A$ is a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, henselian local, with algebraically closed residue field $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A`; $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`), $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hζA`), and $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with the tower $A \to L \to K$. Further, $\varpi$ generates $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   **Chart and supersingular point.** $j \in K$ is nonzero and has Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant. Write $C =$ `chartAlgFin A (↥K) j` for the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and `jChartFin A (↥K) j` for $j$ viewed in $C$. Finally $y$ is a maximal ideal of $C$ containing $\varpi$ (`hy`, `hϖy`), and `hss` requires that $y$ be a supersingular point: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), that is, every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   Throughout the conclusion, for $\gamma \in SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$ a *level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$* means an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29): for every weight $k$, every pair of modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ and $p_g$ having nonzero Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of $p_f/p_g$, and every $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta)=e^{2\pi i/q}$, the coefficientwise image of $\tau x$ under $\iota$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k \bigl(\begin{smallmatrix} a & b/q \\ qc & d\end{smallmatrix}\bigr)$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k \bigl(\begin{smallmatrix} a & b/q \\ qc & d\end{smallmatrix}\bigr)$, where $\bigl(\begin{smallmatrix} a & b \\ c & d\end{smallmatrix}\bigr) = \gamma^{-1}$. Also [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) denotes the quotient of the polynomial ring in two variables over $\kappa$ by the ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q κ - 1`, [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) the kernel of the character $(g,c) \mapsto \overline{\det g}\cdot c^{q+1}$ on $GL_2(\mathbb{Z}/q) \times \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^{\times}$, and `hAction q κ` the resulting action of that subgroup by $\kappa$-algebra automorphisms of the coordinate ring; `redQ q γ` is the reduction of $\gamma$ in $GL_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ and `diagOneElem q d` the matrix $\mathrm{diag}(1,d)$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist an $A$-subalgebra $B \subseteq K$ and a valuation subring $W \subseteq K$ with $B \subseteq W$, such that all of the following hold.
--
--   *(i) Chart properties.* $C \subseteq B$; every $f \in K$ is of the form $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$, $h \ne 0$ (so $K$ is the fraction field of $B$); $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$; and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$.
--
--   *(ii) The valuation ring.* For $x \in L$, the image of $x$ lies in $W$ if and only if $x$ lies in the image of $A$; $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$; $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; for $b \in C$ one has $b \in y$ if and only if the image of $b$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ (so $W$ is centred on $y$); and $f \in W$ if and only if $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$ (so $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak{m}_W \cap B$).
--
--   *(iii) Drinfeld-curve quotient with linked scalars.* For every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$ there is a ring homomorphism $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) which is surjective, has $\rho(b)=0$ exactly when $b \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, and sends $a \in A$ to the image of its residue in $\kappa$; moreover, for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$ (i.e. $f \in W \iff \tau f \in W$), there is $c \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^{\times}$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}_q(\gamma), c) \in$ `hSubgroup q` such that $\rho(\tau b) =$ `hAction` of $(\mathrm{redQ}_q(\gamma),c)$ applied to $\rho(b)$ for all $b \in B$ with $\tau b \in B$; if in addition $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$ then $c \ne 1$; and the scalar $c$ is also realised with trivial linear part: there are $\gamma' \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau'$ at $\gamma'^{-1}$ preserving $W$, with $(1,c) \in$ `hSubgroup q`, such that $\rho(\tau' b) =$ `hAction` of $(1,c)$ applied to $\rho(b)$ for all $b \in B$ with $\tau' b \in B$.
--
--   *(iv) Stability and the fibre over $\varpi$.* $B$ is stable under every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. For every prime ideal $Q$ of $B$ containing $\varpi$ there are $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ such that every $b \in B$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ satisfies $\tau b \in B$ and $\tau b \in Q$. If $b \in B$ is such that for all $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\tau b \in B$ one has $\tau b \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, then $\varpi \mid b$ in $B$. Finally, any level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves $y$ (for $b \in C$ with $\tau b \in C$: $b \in y \iff \tau b \in y$) preserves $W$.
--
--   *(v) Inertia, ends and local models.* There exist $n \ge 1$ with $n \mid q+1$; $\gamma_0 \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau_0$ at $\gamma_0^{-1}$ preserving $W$; $m \ge 1$ with $\varpi^m = \varpi_t w$ for a unit $w$; $\zeta_0$ in the adic completion $\hat A$ of $A$ with $\zeta_0^n = 1$ and $\zeta_0^k - 1$ a unit for $0<k<n$; the element [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the series obtained from the $j$-expansion over $L$ by multiplying all exponents by $q$) lying in $K$ and even in $C$, together with $a_0 \in A$ such that this element minus $a_0$ lies in $y$; and a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K$, such that:
--
--   — $\tau_0^n$ fixes $B$ pointwise, while for each $0<k<n$ some $f \in B$ has $\tau_0^k f \ne f$; every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W$ agrees on $B$ with $\tau_0^k$ for some $k<n$ (the stabiliser acts on $B$ as the cyclic group of order $n$ generated by $\tau_0$);
--
--   — `ends` has exactly $q+1$ elements; every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W$ permutes them (for $O \in$ `ends` there is $O' \in$ `ends` with $f \in O \iff \tau f \in O'$); the action is transitive (for all $O, O' \in$ `ends` there are $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$ with $f \in O \iff \tau f \in O'$); $\tau_0$ fixes each $O$; and distinct $O \ne O'$ are separated by an element belonging to both which is a non-unit of $O$ and a unit of $O'$;
--
--   — there is an $A$-subalgebra $B_c \subseteq K$ of finite type over $A$, stable under all level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, with $B_c \subseteq O$ and $O$ equal to the set of $g/h$ with $g,h \in B_c$ and $h$ a unit of $O$, for every $O \in$ `ends`;
--
--   — for $O \in$ `ends`, $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$: if $\tau(O) \subseteq W$ then $\tau$ preserves $W$;
--
--   — each $O \in$ `ends` satisfies $O \subseteq W$ and is a Noetherian local ring with: $C \subseteq O$; $O \cap L = A$ (an element of $L$ lies in $O$ exactly when it lies in the image of $A$); every $f \in O$ differs from the image of some $a \in A$ by a non-unit of $O$ (the residue field of $O$ is that of $A$); and, with $\varpi \in O$, there are $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $O$ onto `UVCrossingModel` $\hat A\,(\varpi^m)$, that is $\hat A[[U,V]]/(UV - \varpi^m)$, units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ and an $\hat A$-algebra automorphism $\theta_0$ of that model, and $\zeta_0'$ with $\zeta_0\zeta_0'=1$, the model being local, such that: $c_x c_y = \varpi^m u$ in $O$; $\iota$ carries the image of each $a \in A$ to the constant `const` of its image in $\hat A$; $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U\,U$ and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V\,V$; $c_y$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ and $c_x$ does not; the element `jqNModC L q` $- a_0$ lies in $O$ and $\iota$ carries it to $w_V V^e$ for some unit $w_V$ and some $e \ge 1$; $\iota$ intertwines $\tau_0$ with $\theta_0$ (for $f \in O$ with $\tau_0 f \in O$); and $\theta_0(U) - \mathrm{const}(\zeta_0)\,U$ and $\theta_0(V) - \mathrm{const}(\zeta_0')\,V$ both lie in the square of the maximal ideal of the model;
--
--   — in addition, for each such $O$ there is a valuation subring $W_x \subseteq K$ with: $O \subseteq W_x$; $C \subseteq W_x$; $W_x \cap L = A$; $W_x$ a discrete valuation ring with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ generated by $\varpi$; an element $t \in W_x$ such that no polynomial over $A$ with a coefficient outside $\mathfrak{m}_A$ takes a value in $\mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ at $t$, and the same separation property for the element `jqNModC L q` (its residue is transcendental over $\kappa$); $c_x \in \mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ and $c_y \notin \mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$; every $b \in C$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ lies in $y$, while some $b \in y$ is not in $\mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$; every other end $O' \ne O$ contains an element not in $W_x$; and for $O' \in$ `ends` and any level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, $\tau(O') \subseteq W_x$ forces $O' = O$;
--
--   — and an $A$-subalgebra $B_x \subseteq K$ with $B_x \subseteq B \cap O$, of finite type over $A$, stable under all level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, such that every $f \in B_x$ has $P.\mathrm{ord}(f) \ge 0$ at each place $P$ of $K$ over $L$ with $P.\mathrm{ord}(j) \ge 0$; $O$ is the set of $g/h$ with $g,h \in B_x$ and $h$ a unit of $O$; and some $b \in B_x$ has the property that for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ with $V \cap L = A$, with $\varpi \in \mathfrak{m}_V$, with $j \in V$ and no monic polynomial in $j$ over $A$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_V$, and with $O \not\subseteq V$, one has $b \notin V$;
--
--   — (common chart) every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ with $V \cap L = A$, $C \subseteq V$ and $y \subseteq \mathfrak{m}_V$ either contains $B$, or there is $O \in$ `ends` with $O \subseteq V$ and every non-unit of $O$ in $\mathfrak{m}_V$;
--
--   — (orbit poles) some $b \in B$ satisfies $b \notin V$ for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ with $V \cap L = A$, $\varpi \in \mathfrak{m}_V$, $j \in V$ and no monic polynomial in $j$ over $A$ in $\mathfrak{m}_V$;
--
--   — (separation of other orbits) for every maximal ideal $y''$ of $C$ containing $\varpi$ which is not matched with $y$ by any level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, there is $b \in B$ such that for every such $\gamma$ and $\tau$ and every valuation subring $V \subseteq K$ containing $C$ and such that each $c \in C$ with $\tau^{-1}(c) \in y''$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_V$, one has $b \notin V$.
--
--   *(vi) Drinfeld-curve quotient with tame inertia.* For every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$ there is a homomorphism $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with all the properties listed in (iii) — surjectivity, kernel $\mathfrak{m}_W \cap B$, compatibility with $A \to \kappa$, $\Gamma_0(M')$-equivariance with nontrivial scalars on $\Gamma(q)$ and linked scalars — and in addition there is $\eta \in \{1,q\}$ such that the following holds. Let $\pi \in A$ satisfy $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$; let $\sigma_L$ and $\sigma_A$ be ring automorphisms of $L$ and of $A$ compatible with $A \to L$ and with $\sigma_A a \equiv a \pmod{\mathfrak{m}_A}$ for all $a$; let $\tilde\alpha \in A$ with $\sigma_A \pi = \tilde\alpha\,\pi$, and $\alpha \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^{\times}$ whose image in $\kappa$ is the residue of $\tilde\alpha$; and let $\tau$ be a ring automorphism of $K$ acting on Laurent expansions coefficientwise by $\sigma_L$. Then $\tau$ preserves $B$ and preserves $W$, and for every $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/q)^{\times}$ whose image in $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ equals $\alpha^{q+1}$, with $(\mathrm{diag}(1,(d^{\eta})^{-1}), \alpha^{\eta}) \in$ `hSubgroup q`, one has $\rho(\tau b) =$ `hAction` of $(\mathrm{diag}(1,(d^{\eta})^{-1}),\alpha^{\eta})$ applied to $\rho(b)$ for all $b \in B$ with $\tau b \in B$.
--
--   The clause (iii) is thus asserted twice, once on its own and once as part of the strengthened clause (vi).
--
--   This packages the local structure, over a henselian discrete valuation ring $A$ with algebraically closed residue field, of the integral model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M') \cap \Gamma_1(\ell)$ at a supersingular point in characteristic $q$: a formally smooth chart $B$ with a Drinfeld-curve description of its special fibre, the $q+1$ branches ("ends") through the crossing point with their $\hat A[[U,V]]/(UV-\varpi^m)$ models, the cyclic inertia of order dividing $q+1$, and the tame action of automorphisms coming from the base. It is the small-prime (auxiliary level) form of the chart statement, and is used in the constructions of semistable data for $q = 3$ and $q = 2$ carried out in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_inertia_of_levelField_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_inertia_of_levelField_of_eq_three_of_dvd) and `…_of_eq_two_of_dvd`.
